														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2680101">
									

<p>Patina and rust also develop this smell naturally from reactions with atmospheric particles (dust, aromatic/volatile compounds, etc.). Direct contact with them just makes it stronger.</p>
<p>I'm very fond of the smell myself thanks to working summers at a salvage yard while I was in high school. Lots of rusty metal reacting with petroleum residue and decaying polymers&#8230; aspiring mad scientist heaven. Comes back to me every time I watch Mad Max movies, play a Fallout game, or paint something dieselpunk.</p>

